---
title: Table forms
---

# Ways to make a table

This renderer builds tables from Markdown **pipe tables** (optionally wrapped
in a `table` tag for styling), shown below. The Markdoc **list-syntax** table
(cells as `*` items separated by `---`) is also supported — see
`table-list-syntax`.

## Basic table

A plain pipe table. The first row is the header.

| Heading 1    | Heading 2    |
|--------------|--------------|
| Row 1 Cell 1 | Row 1 Cell 2 |
| Row 2 Cell 1 | Row 2 Cell 2 |

## Table without a header

Leave the header row blank (`| | |`) and it is dropped, leaving a plain grid.

| | |
|------|------|
| foo  | bar  |
| foo  | bar  |

## Header column (row headers)

Wrap the table in a `table` tag with `header_column=true` to turn the first
column into row headers (bold + shaded).

{% table header_column=true %}
| | |
|---------|------------|
| Date    | 2026-05-20 |
| Version | 3.9.0      |
| Author  | MiR        |
{% /table %}

## Text alignment

Use CommonMark column markers in the delimiter row — `:---` left,
`:--:` centre, `---:` right.

| Left        | Centre | Right |
|:------------|:------:|------:|
| foo         | bar    | baz   |
| another row | mid    | 1,234 |
| x           | y      | 42    |
